      "phase": "preparation",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Build a serial structural candidate: normalize dimensions so c=min(M,N) is the paired axis, transpose logically when needed, and scan r=max(M,N). Store logical columns contiguously, increment a reusable r-element projection for each right boundary, and retain the exact prefix-sum counting method. This removes the rectangular-shape penalty of O(M*N^2) and improves locality; use generic fast input, keep the answer int64, and measure it without threading.",
        "B": "Own the prefix-frequency hot kernel. Replace per-pair unordered_map clearing/node allocation and repeated lookup with a preallocated open-addressed table sized for at most r+1 prefixes, with robust hashing, probing, and epoch/touched-slot reset. Query count(s-k) before incrementing count(s); support negatives and never allocate by the potentially ~2e9 key range. Make it drop-in for A's layout, preserve int64 answers, and compare against a reserved unordered_map baseline.",
        "C": "Develop the shared-memory candidate for the exact paired-boundary scan. Split outer left-boundary work across at most four workers using triangular-weighted ranges (or measure a low-overhead dynamic alternative), with private projection arrays, hash tables, and local int64 totals followed by reduction. Add a generic sequential fallback for too little work; do not share mutable counting state or assume balanced plain static chunks.",
        "G": "Integrate only measured, valid candidates. Benchmark baseline, each tree output, and coherent layout/kernel/thread combinations on the same harness; validate each against the existing oracle before selection. Do not assume gains compose: retain the fastest valid variant, including baseline if necessary, while preserving generic correctness, unchanged build/target constraints, and clean single-line output.",
        "analysis": "The verified baseline takes 0.249738 s and is an O(M*N^2) column-pair scan whose dominant avoidable costs are orientation blindness and unordered_map work in every pair. Arbitrary negative entries rule out sliding-window shortcuts; the exact prefix-frequency algorithm remains necessary, and the submatrix count requires int64. The four-core ARM target makes a carefully isolated shared-memory variant worthwhile, but cache/layout, hash, and threading changes must be evaluated independently."
      },
